+### `drain(count)` -> `array`
+
+Remove items from the front of the queue and return them in FIFO order. If `count` is omitted or `undefined`, all items are removed. An explicit `count` must be a finite, nonnegative integer; a count larger than the queue length removes all available items. A count of zero returns an empty array without changing the queue.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1,2,3,4]);
+denque.drain(2); // [1,2]
+denque.toArray(); // [3,4]
+denque.drain(); // [3,4]
+```
+
+
+
 ### `toArray()` -> `Array`
 
 Returns the items in the queue as an array. Starting from the item in the front of the queue and ending to the item at the back of the queue.
